{"kind":"request","text":"Prove whether failed claims can close a register\n\nFrom the planner's cccd205a, second fact of 1f8fecbc. A claim with three failed attempts stays pending and counts toward max: 64, so 64 such claims refuse every later found. Run this on real scopes. If it runs as read, a host outage can close a register, and the planner gives it priority over the other facts. Done when a run shows the result, the report states what a person sees and what frees a place, and the planner has it. A repair follows the planner's ruling on that report.","body":{"conditions":"a run on real scopes shows the result, and the planner has the report","target_head":"970c701c72d5ceb1de8a09294ae2d1ddaaff4a8e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}